# Opening the test app

When Timka asks to run, rebuild, or reopen the app, open it on the booted iPhone 17 simulator. This Xcode has no Simulator.app. The window is Device Hub.

- Simulator UDID: `3DD6E11D-675E-4AE8-86F6-5FAC411B49BA`
- The installed dev client bundle id is `com.timothykossenkov.miple`. `mobile/app.json` still says `com.miple.app` for the shared project. Do not change that shared id. Relaunch whatever bundle id is actually installed.
- Metro: from `mobile/`, `unset CI`, PATH includes `/opt/homebrew/bin`, then `npx expo start --dev-client --port 8081`. Leave it running.
- `simctl` and Device Hub need to run outside the sandbox.

Do not `simctl launch` the app by itself. That lands on "Searching for development servers."

```bash
xcrun simctl terminate 3DD6E11D-675E-4AE8-86F6-5FAC411B49BA com.timothykossenkov.miple || true
xcrun simctl openurl 3DD6E11D-675E-4AE8-86F6-5FAC411B49BA "exp+miple://expo-development-client/?url=http%3A%2F%2F127.0.0.1%3A8081"
open "devices://device/open?id=3DD6E11D-675E-4AE8-86F6-5FAC411B49BA"
```

A native change (icon, HealthKit, new native module) needs a rebuild, then the same open:

```bash
cd mobile && npx expo run:ios --device 3DD6E11D-675E-4AE8-86F6-5FAC411B49BA --no-bundler
```

Use the phone (`00008140-001E48A40247001C`, name `timka`) only when Timka asks for the phone. The simulator has no camera; receipt tests use Choose from library.
